What is the Roud Folk Song Index, and how is it used to catalog and identify traditional folk songs, including nursery rhymes?
The Roud Folk Song Index is a database of around 250,000 references to nearly 25,000 traditional folk songs collected from oral tradition in the English language from all over the world. It is compiled by Steve Roud and serves as a comprehensive cataloging system for traditional folk songs, including nursery rhymes. The index combines printed sources (such as the Broadside Index) with a field-recording index, and it subsumes all the previous printed sources known to Francis James Child (the Child Ballads), as well as recordings from 1900 to 1975. This allows users to identify and locate specific traditional songs, including those like "Pat-a-cake, pat-a-cake, baker's man" (Roud Folk Song Index number 6486) and "The Muffin Man" (Roud Folk Song Index number 7922).
