What is the historical context and significance of the name 'Mountbatten-Windsor' in the European royal dynasties?
The name 'Mountbatten-Windsor' is significant in the European royal dynasties as it represents the personal surname used by some of the male-line descendants of Queen Elizabeth II and Prince Philip, Duke of Edinburgh. This name was declared in Privy Council in 1960, indicating that it has a specific historical context tied to the British monarchy's lineage and succession.

In essence, the name 'Mountbatten-Windsor' signifies the connection to the House of Windsor, which is the current royal house of the United Kingdom, while also acknowledging the contribution of Prince Philip's family name, Mountbatten. This name is used by descendants of the Queen who do not hold royal styles and titles, highlighting the importance of lineage and succession within the European royal dynasties.
